"hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2816,"Muhammad bin Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad bin Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us, Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ziyad, who is Ibn Sa'd, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu Ma'bad, from Ibn Abbas (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Remove the harm from the belly of Urnah, and remove the harm from the belly of Muhassir."""
2817,"###
 Abdullah bin Hashim narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Sa'id narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: 'Ata' informed me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (RA), who said: It used to be said: ""Keep away from Muhassir, and keep away from Urana."" As for the statement ""Urana,"" it refers to standing at Urana, meaning they should not stand at Urana. And as for the statement ""Muhassir,"" it refers to stopping at Jam"
2818,"Narrated to us 'Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-'Ala', narrated to us Sufyan, who said: I memorized it from 'Amr, from 'Amr ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Safwan, who informed us Yazid ibn Shayban—who is his maternal uncle—who said:

Ibn Mirba' al-Ansari came to us while we were standing at 'Arafah behind the place of standing, which 'Amr had distanced from the standing place. He said, ""I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to you.""

**CHAPTER:**"
2819,"###
 Narrated to us Abu 'Ammar Al-Husayn ibn Hurayth and Sa'id ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, who said: Narrated to us Sufyan, from 'Amr (who is Ibn Dinar), from 'Amr ibn 'Abdullah ibn Safwan, from Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Shihab. Abu 'Ammar added: And we were informed by Yazid ibn Shayban, who said: We were standing at a place behind the standing place ("
